From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:57:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] clk: samsung: exynos7870: model CMU_CPUCL0 and
 CMU_CPUCL1

Model the two CPU cluster CMUs (CPUCL0 at 0x10900000, CPUCL1 at
0x10800000, note the inverted address order) after the existing
CMU_G3D block, plus the CLKCMU_CPUCL0/1_SWITCH divider and gate pairs
in CMU_MIF (0x458/0x45c and 0x858/0x85c, twins of the G3D switch that
is already modelled), and add the two CMU nodes to the SoC dtsi.

Registers, mux/div/gate topology and bit positions follow the vendor
pwrcal sources (S5E7870-cmu.c, S5E7870-cmusfr.h) and were checked
against a register dump of the state S-BOOT leaves: both PLLs at
902.2 MHz (M=347, P=5, S=1), the CLK_CPUCLx muxes on the PLL branch and
MUX_STAT reading sel+1.

The PLL rate table holds all 17 P/M/S tuples of the ECT PLL block
(identical for the two clusters), with the exact rates rather than the
rounded vendor names.  Which of them can actually be reached is left to
the CPU clock configuration data and the OPP tables.

All dividers are modelled read-only.  On the CPU and debug path they
are level-independent in the ECT DVFS block; the one exception is HPM,
which the vendor reprograms per level (/5, /4, /3) and which is left at
its boot value of /4: at the top usable level that is 1586/4 =
396.5 MHz, below the 400.4 MHz the vendor itself feeds this sensor,
which is unused here anyway.

S-BOOT leaves the user mux of the switch branch on OSCCLK.  The CPU
clock parks the cores on that branch while the PLL relocks, so the
dtsi assigns the CMU_MIF switch gate as its parent: without it the
cores would drop to 26 MHz instead of 800 MHz during a relock.

Nothing consumes the cluster clocks yet and no rate changes at boot.

The new CMU_MIF clock IDs (129-132) are appended out of alphabetical
order to keep the existing numbering; the new CPUCL0 and CPUCL1
sections follow the alphabetical order of the header.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---

Notes:
